course: dictionary
lesson: 13556
title: Thinking before acting
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Impulsively is an adverb. It tells you how someone did something: they acted suddenly, without stopping to think first. «Mia impulsively grabbed the last cake from the plate.» Mia did not wait or think. She just grabbed it.
explain: Read the words around it to find its meaning. Clues like a sudden wish, a quick action, or a decision made in a rush often sit near it. «Sam saw the new game and impulsively bought it with all his pocket money.» He had a sudden wish, so he acted before he thought.
explain: Impulsively is often a warning word. Acting impulsively can lead to something you regret later, like spending all your savings on one thing. A good habit is stop, think, then act. To check your meaning, put «suddenly, without thinking» into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Impulsively means suddenly and without stopping to think first.
fact: It can also mean following a strong sudden wish or feeling, often in a way you may regret later.
fact: Impulsively is an adverb, so it tells us how someone does an action: «She impulsively shouted across the playground.»
fact: Shops often place sweets near the till because people buy impulsively.
fact: Useful phrases: act impulsively, buy impulsively, impulsively decide.
exercise: «Tom saw the puppy in the window and impulsively ran inside to buy it.» What does impulsively mean here? | Sadly, with a heavy heart | *Suddenly, without stopping to think | Quietly, so nobody could hear | Slowly, after a long talk with his family
exercise: Which action shows someone acting impulsively? | Asking a teacher for help after checking the rules | *Grabbing the last biscuit before anyone else can move | Reading the instructions, then slowly choosing a seat | Counting to ten before answering a question
exercise: «Lily impulsively decided to dye her hair green.» Which word shows the decision was sudden? | green | *impulsively | Lily | hair
test: Which word fits best? «Ben ___ spent his savings on a huge bag of sweets.» | politely | slowly | *impulsively | carefully
test: Why do shops put sweets near the till? | *Because people often buy impulsively | Because the till is the only shelf in the shop | Because sweets are heavy and must sit low | Because sweets must be kept warm
exam: Which sentence shows someone acting impulsively? | *Ana shouted the answer before the teacher had finished the question | Ana raised her hand and waited to be asked | Ana checked her work twice before handing it in | Ana counted to ten and then spoke quietly
